code_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coyoteintx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1375273#post1375273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-the-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Savage Age Vol 1</a> </b>snuck back up to number 8 of STV!<br /> <br /> ...and since a lot of us are social distancing and doing the right thing -- here is a discount for Savage Age: Its only $10.00 if you use <b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?discount=9ce1622319\" target=\"_blank\">THIS LINK! </a></b><br /> <br /> <b>So, yeah, $10.00. Enjoy. </b><br /> <br /> I figure if you are a fan of Werewolf and stuck indoors, Savage Age might be a fun read or play.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Purchased! Thanks for the discount!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T17:50:24-07:00","id":1375724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1375508#post1375508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Purchased! Thanks for the discount!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My pleasure. Sorry I cant give a deeper discount. If you like what you see, let me know if you want a discount for the other Savage Age products and I'll post some here for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 03-19-2020, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T13:47:59-07:00","id":1375854,"title":"","content":"<b>WiP of Savage Age Volume 2:</b><br /> <br /> The War of Rage was not a singular event. The first conflicts that would evolve into the world-wide war started in the Indian subcontinent between the Grondr and the Kucha Sukurai. The rivalry between the boar- and dhole-shifters preceded the War of Rage by generations, but evolved into a genocidal conflict around 16,000 years ago. The Grondr and the Kucha Sakurai were both very prideful and competitive people, and their rivalries became deadly generations-long blood feuds. The conflict increased in severity and viciousness with each generation, as each side built a long litany of perceived wrongs and decades-old grievances. <br /> <br /> In time, the numbers of both type of Fera in the subcontinent began to suffer. Neither side could gain a decisive advantage for long, and the body count continued to climb. Rather than deescalate, the Kucha Sakurai called on old alliances with wolf- and canid-shifters to bolster their numbers. The Grondr sought aid from other Fera, including the Apis. <br /> <br /> The involvement of multiple types of Fera and the expansion of the conflict past the sub-continent marked the true beginning of the War of Rage. <br /> <br /> The conflict spread to the Near East, Europe and Africa. Ironically, as those wars increased and widened, the conflict between the Grondr and the Kucha Sakurai gradually tapered off. Unfortunately, the cycle of generational grievances and reprisals spread like a virus and became entrenched in the other continents. <br /> <br /> The legacy of the War of Rage remains unprecedented. The Grondr, Apis, Saksom Aknami, and Weiewa were driven into extinction. The Khara were forced to seek refuge in the Americas, and were set on the path to extinction. The Celican were forced into slavery into Arcadia and presumed dead. The Bastet and Mokole would suffer significant losses on all three continents. The Naghaluu avoided the War proper, but still paid a dear price for the lingering animosities it engendered in Fera survivors.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation was born in the crucible of the War of Rage. The pack-focused nature canid- and wolf-shifters gave them an important advantage over the other Fera. The canid-Fera could work together across fairly significant social, linguistic, and cultural divides that prevented the other Fera from pooling their resources. When one branch of the newly-formed Garou Nation faltered, there were always others to pick up the slack. <br /> <br /> In the Savage Age, the Garou Nation was a radical and unproven social experiment. The word \u2018Garou\u2019 was a social term, not a biological one. The Garou Nation of the Savage Age was akin to the beast courts of modern nights. It was only until much, much later that the term Garou referred to not only the cosmopolitan alliance of Tribes but also the wolf-shifters themselves. In the Savage Age, the wolf-shifters still have their own names for their peoples and only identify as Garou after they note their ancestry first. <br /> <br /> The wolf-shifters also paid a heavy price for their participation War of Rage. The Atzu Telal Nahau splintered into three rival groups as a result of their actions in the War of Rage. The Bilai suffered massive losses that would take generations to recover from. The Siberakh would undergo their own civil war generations later that was a legacy of the War of Rage. The Anupu-Ba-El and Kucha would be absorbed into the Garou Nation and struggle to keep their cultural identities. The War of Rage also removed any chance to add the Naghaluu and Tengger to the Garou\u2019s ranks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T12:27:00-07:00","id":1376135,"title":"","content":"Additional Question<br /> <br /> Sorry, but could you tell me how can I become one of writers just like you? How do you recruit?<br /> <br /> I want to contribute to this project. Could you PM?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 03-22-2020, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T11:26:37-07:00","id":1385273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1376135#post1376135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Additional Question<br /> <br /> Sorry, but could you tell me how can I become one of writers just like you? How do you recruit?<br /> <br /> I want to contribute to this project. Could you PM?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Apologies -- just saw this. Happy to send you a PM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T12:50:22-07:00","id":1385284,"title":"","content":"So, the legendary Mr. Gone gave the new form fillable / editable <b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/311674/Werewolf-the-Savage-Age-Fillable-Character-Sheet\" target=\"_blank\">character sheet for Savage Age</a></b> a strong thumb's up. How great is that? <br /> <br /> That seriously made my day. Getting that project done as both a normal and editable sheet has been a major undertaking. I hated using the Dark Ages character sheet -- it was good enough, but didnt reflect the differences that Savage Age embraces in terms of game play. I put off doing a character sheet for a long time, prioritizing other things -- until I finally got fed up. I am super glad its there.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T05:25:50-07:00","id":1386661,"title":"","content":"So... after a lot of work... <b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/Werewolf-the-Savage-Age-Volume-2\" target=\"_blank\">Savage Age Volume 2: the Rise of the Garou</a></b> is up! Focuses on four new proto Garou &quot;Tribes,&quot; a new Gurahl type, lots of discussion on Totems appropriate to the Pleistocene, stories, and an essay on the conditions that led to the formation of the Garou. It also has the new snazzy character sheet (though thats free on STV). <br /> <br /> As WtA fans, I would really appreciate any feedback (good or bad). I was up late last night working on the STV page and once I woke up this morning realized I forgot to add in some content (tiruals) -- so that is still coming. I'll probably wait a week or so while I go through the manuscripts and find any spelling/layout errors and clean them up -- then add in the rituals.<br /> <br /> I also have two more large-ish pieces of art coming - one showing an Imperial Moot and another showing a Bilai warrior-chronicler standing triumphant in a battle zone. <br /> <br /> What it doesn't have is Fetishes or Talens (neither did Vol 1). Thats going to be one of the next projects -- a small-ish book on special tools and magic items appropriate to the Savage Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T04:48:36-07:00","id":1386951,"title":"","content":"Its all pretty excellent stuff ( I haven't grabbed Vol. 2 just yet.), but my only boggle with it is that like Shattered Dreams did to the the Ananasi in making them All Arsehole, All The Time. Savage Age has Mokole playing that role of irredeemable scumbag.....which is probably not a big issue for most folks but they're kinda my faves. So it makes me sad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But as I said. Excellent work all round.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T06:45:07-07:00","id":1386967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1386951#post1386951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its all pretty excellent stuff ( I haven't grabbed Vol. 2 just yet.), but my only boggle with it is that like Shattered Dreams did to the the Ananasi in making them All Arsehole, All The Time. Savage Age has Mokole playing that role of irredeemable scumbag.....which is probably not a big issue for most folks but they're kinda my faves. So it makes me sad. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I wrote in the Mokole parts not to make them jerks all the time, but because they were from my perspective, a bit too alabaster and pure. I wanted the Mokole to have a bit more dimension to them. With all that power and knowledge and experience, I wanted to explore their dark side. I also wanted to address their possession of dinosaur shapes eve though they are not really connected to the dinosaurs -- so how did that happen? Likewise, why is the Corax 'war' form so pathetic when they come from some of the most impressive creatures ever? <br /> <br /> That said, the Mokole are far from irredeemable. In Khara they play a key role in keep the sabretooths alive (for at least a bit longer) in both the old world and the new. By the time the Khara and Balam exact their misplaced revenge against the Naghaluu, the Mokole are just... tired. I also think that they make the hard choice of standing aside and letting that fight play out. It saddens them deeply, but to keep the long-term peace in the new world they do not intervene. (thats all in the background, though)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But as I said. Excellent work all round. </div> </div> </div>I greatly appreciate it. <br /> <br /> Out of curiosity... where the line to address the Mokole in a deeper fashion, any advice on the direction you would like to see them go? I'll admit they are far from my favorite Fera, but I would like to hear thoughts from someone that considers them boss. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T16:39:16-07:00","id":1389113,"title":"","content":"I liked the Mokole in their Breedbook and truly hated the way they were retconned in PGttCB and CB20, as Red Talons with scales who plan to wipe out humanity. The only thing CB20 did right was make the wereturtles interesting instead of a joke, and show Mokole casually eating humans who attack them.<br /> <br /> The Mokole Breedbook explains quite clearly why the Mnesis and their own history gives Mokole a connection to dinosaurs. It's straightforward and very cool. I loved the overall idea of the Age of Kings, of shapeshifter species millions of years older than humanity -- despite the problems with the Bird Kings, Pouch Kings, and Sal-Afsan concepts. PGttCB retconned all the Age of Kings to nothing but lies and hallucinations caused by <b>mitochondria</b>, besides badly messing up the Mokole form statistics, auspices, and Gifts. I would not want to buy a series that perpetuates those retcons and errors, or makes the Mokole all evil. They don't even have a reason to be as aggressive as the Garou, on average. Aloof, alien, callous, and not clear on why they suddenly need to cooperate with these new Bete, sure. Pure evil.... no. Why?<br /> <br /> As for the Corax warform, they aren't warriors and they aren't weredragons. They're wereravens and scouts who are not designed to fight. Their warform should be 1. weak and 2. based solely on ravens. The Mokole archid form is unique because nobody else has Mnesis.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> About canid shifters, I urge you to carefully research the animals involved before writing a book about Garou being an amalgam of wolves and &quot;jackals&quot;. The widespread and dominant North African canid is <i>Canis anthous</i>, the golden wolf, <b>not</b> a jackal. For a long time it was mistakenly considered a golden jackal, but it is in fact a wolf. It is much more similar to the grey wolves than it is to the golden jackal, let alone the side-striped and black-backed jackals which should be in a separate genus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Lastly, I reccommend that you avoid using anachronistic names from modern languages. &quot;Kucha Ekundu&quot;, for example, is probably a word in a modern language and it refers to African wild dogs, not dholes. It doesn't make sense to me that you chopped the name in half and used &quot;Kucha&quot; for Ice Age dholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 05-16-2020, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T13:10:15-07:00","id":1390048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1389113#post1389113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I liked the Mokole in their Breedbook and truly hated the way they were retconned in PGttCB and CB20, as Red Talons with scales who plan to wipe out humanity. The only thing CB20 did right was make the wereturtles interesting instead of a joke, and show Mokole casually eating humans who attack them.<br /> <br /> The Mokole Breedbook explains quite clearly why the Mnesis and their own history gives Mokole a connection to dinosaurs. It's straightforward and very cool. I loved the overall idea of the Age of Kings, of shapeshifter species millions of years older than humanity -- despite the problems with the Bird Kings, Pouch Kings, and Sal-Afsan concepts. PGttCB retconned all the Age of Kings to nothing but lies and hallucinations caused by <b>mitochondria</b>, besides badly messing up the Mokole form statistics, auspices, and Gifts. I would not want to buy a series that perpetuates those retcons and errors, or makes the Mokole all evil. They don't even have a reason to be as aggressive as the Garou, on average. Aloof, alien, callous, and not clear on why they suddenly need to cooperate with these new Bete, sure. Pure evil.... no. Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of making them alien and reserved -- because their memories are ancient and function differently than the other Fera. Thats something I have wanted to push for a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the Corax warform, they aren't warriors and they aren't weredragons. They're wereravens and scouts who are not designed to fight. Their warform should be 1. weak and 2. based solely on ravens. The Mokole archid form is unique because nobody else has Mnesis </div> </div> </div>The goal with looking at the Corax again is to reconcile their connect to archosaurs and dinosurs (specifically). Sure, now they are messengers... but the bird-dinosaur connection suggests they might come from a longer line of Fera with deeper roots than just their modern kin. I figure that might be something fun to explore and tweak a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About canid shifters, I urge you to carefully research the animals involved before writing a book about Garou being an amalgam of wolves and &quot;jackals&quot;. The widespread and dominant North African canid is <i>Canis anthous</i>, the golden wolf, <b>not</b> a jackal. For a long time it was mistakenly considered a golden jackal, but it is in fact a wolf. It is much more similar to the grey wolves than it is to the golden jackal, let alone the side-striped and black-backed jackals which should be in a separate genus. </div> </div> </div>I appreciate where you are coming from -- but it should be noted the Anupu are from jackals. The Anupu of the Savage Age are related to Canis aureus and C. adustus, not Canis anthus. Down the line, i was thinking about using C. anthus (and the himilayan wolf) as an lost branch of the Nuwisha... but thats a different book (it might fit as a hook for playing Nuwisha in Europe and the War of Rage for the player's guide).<br /> <br /> The Nahau get some <i>C. Anthus</i> love since they are also, generally, from the region but the Anupu are very specifically jackals.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, the Anupu in the Savage Age serve as a one of the examples of how the 'Garou&quot; started off as a multi-Fera social club (so to speak). The founders of the Garou Nation include jackals, wild dogs, Beringian wolves, grey wolves, (some dholes), etc. Then, over time, the heterogeneity of the various members of the Garou Nation start to winnow down so that the likes of the Anupu and Kucha assimilate biologically and increasingly adopt lupus kin... leading us to the modern Garou Nation which blurs the lines between the boundaries of the social and biological nature of the werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, I reccommend that you avoid using anachronistic names from modern languages. &quot;Kucha Ekundu&quot;, for example, is probably a word in a modern language and it refers to African wild dogs, not dholes. It doesn't make sense to me that you chopped the name in half and used &quot;Kucha&quot; for Ice Age dholes. </div> </div> </div>We decided to use nomenclature that people would recognize since trying to recreate language from 10,000 y/a isa bit of a fool's errand for a game book. For example, Kucha is a term that players steeped in the lore will immediately recognize and using that info, be able to make some connections about the Savage Age's presentation. Its the same reason we used 'Siberakh' - because it has very specific connections to W:tA. Basically, its a useful shorthand. Its also the same reason we use modern location names throughout the books -- its just easier and getting into the minutiae doesnt really help the book or people's understanding of whats going on (quite the opposite, actually). I bring this up the notes in Savage Age Vol 1.<br /> <br /> Also, per your question about the Wild Dog and Dhole connection -- the two were likely derived from C xenocyon (or, at least, thats what the preponderance of science suggests). The complexities of the C. xenocyon to Cuon/Lycaon connection gets some wordcount in Savage Age Vol 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 05-19-2020, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T19:32:01-07:00","id":1417237,"title":"","content":"The Savage Age line keeps chugging along! <b><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction: Volume Three</a></b> is available now. Its all about deepening the resources available to players and Storytellers and is designed to complement (and enhance) existing characters and chronicles. New fetishes and talens. New types of totems. Essays. Stories. We designed it to be as useful for Apocalypse players as Savage Age ones. <br /> <br /> Happy to answer any questions or issues that you all may have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-10T08:05:35-07:00","id":1417547,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">So, with Tools of Extinction out, I want to encourage any Werewolf players that might be interested in the line to pick it up.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">Accounting for the Dead and Rise of the Garou are the two &quot;big&quot; books for the Savage Age. The first goes into depth about the progenitors to the Silent Striders (and, to a lesser extent, the Children of Gaia), the Apis, Grondr, and gives an overview of the Khara (were-sabretooths). There are also rules for playing Neanderthals. It serves as the entry point to the setting, with a lot of advice about how to mechanically represent the stane age/Pleistocene.<br /> <br /> Rise of the Garou is designed as a solid companion piece to Accounting for the Dead. It covers the creation of the Garou nation and what it meant to be &quot;Garou&quot; before the Tribes were the Tribes. It talks about the progenitors to the Get, Shadow Lords, Silver Fangs, White Howlers, Fianna, Children of Gaia... as well as the Saaksom Aknami (were CaveBears). There </span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Accounting for the Dead (volume 1) for $10: </span></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?discount=9ce1622319\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/br...unt=9ce1622319</a><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Rise fo the Garou (volume 2) for $8: </span></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?discount=922586ac47\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.storytellersvault.com/br...unt=922586ac47</a></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">There </span>are a number of projects in the works right now...<br /> <br /> <b>Tribebook Wlewa: Werecavelions </b>-- the key opponents to the Garou during the War of Rage. They pay the ultimate price.<br /> <br /> <b>Tribebook [Unnamed]: Werebats</b> -- We are going to look at the Camazotz back before they were &quot;region locked.&quot; Their schtick is that they defend Gaia from hostile &quot;star entities&quot; -- creatures from the Deep Umbra that seek to hurt Gaia and advamnce their own alien agendas (lots of Rage Across the Heavens goodness).<br /> <br /> <b>A Look At the Umbra -</b>- just as it sounds. The Triat is VERY different in this age, with the Wyld being the primary challenge and the Weaver making important inroads to civiliation and agriculture. Likewise, the Destroyer Wyrm isnt completely annihilated.<br /> <br /> <b>Rage Across the Stone Age </b>-- will touch on the canon shifters we havent discussed so far. The other Bastet, the Mokole, the Nagah, the Ratkin, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":11548,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","user":"Coyoteintx","date":". 10-10-2020, 11:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-03T05:18:16-08:00","id":1421598,"title":"","content":"Hi. Just found this topic after being a long time follower of you on the Vault. I've really enjoyed all your stuff so far and I'm looking forward to the future projects you described (especially the werebats. RAtH ftw!).<br /> <br /> Thank you for your work!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15685-up-to-eleven","name":"Up-to-Eleven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T05:17:22-08:00","id":1424521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Up-to-Eleven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1421598#post1421598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi. Just found this topic after being a long time follower of you on the Vault. I've really enjoyed all your stuff so far and I'm looking forward to the future projects you described (especially the werebats. RAtH ftw!).<br /> <br /> Thank you for your work!</div> </div> </div> </div>I really appreciate hearing that. The Savage Age has been a labor of love (and not insignificant cost I probably will never recover). <br /> <br /> ...and yeah, the Bats are going to be cool. I do a lot of horror freelancing, and am going to channel some of that. Its also a great way to explore the really dark areas of the deep celestial Umbra. Shoot an email to us at the weaponizedink address and I will make sure you get a head's up when it releases (its still months away, though) <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-17T05:18:03-08:00","id":1424522,"title":"","content":"...and we now have a jumpstart/quickstart for the Savage Age! We designed this to make it easy to get right into a chronicle. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336263/The-Savage-Age-Epic-Jumpstart-The-BrokenBrother\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/336263.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336263/The-Savage-Age-Epic-Jumpstart-The-BrokenBrother\" target=\"_blank\"> The Savage Age Epic Jumpstart: The Broken-Brother - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336263/The-Savage-Age-Epic-Jumpstart-The-BrokenBrother\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/336263/The-Savage-Age-Epic-Jumpstart-The-BrokenBrother </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Savage Age Epic Jumpstart: The Broken-Brother - Start Your Savage Age Chronicle Here.&nbsp;&nbsp; Weaponized Ink is offering prospective players and long-time fans of&nbsp;Werewol </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-27T09:49:26-08:00","id":1426329,"title":"","content":"Hi Christopher,<br /> <br /> I wanted to just remind you about the issue with the Khara book, that I mentioned over on its DriveThru page (posting as Ellen S.)<br /> <br /> Also I'd like to ask about these Cave Lions and Cave Bears -- how similar are they to the canon/modern Simba and Gurahl?<br /> And... have you considered making Bastet tribebooks for the Eurasian Qualmi/Werelynxes, and the <i>Miracinonyx</i> of North America? Or the Okuma?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I feel like I already asked you about your Ceilican but I can't find where. Are yours based on &quot;maneless lions&quot; or on some kinda wildcat?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 11-27-2020, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T14:20:00-07:00","id":1449208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coyoteintx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1417547#post1417547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>A Look At the Umbra -</b>- just as it sounds. The Triat is VERY different in this age, with the Wyld being the primary challenge and the Weaver making important inroads to civiliation and agriculture. Likewise, the Destroyer Wyrm isnt completely annihilated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really excited for this! Is your team open to any new contributors on these projects?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-21T20:39:28-07:00","id":1449225,"title":"","content":"I have recently dived into all the Savage Age lore and will likely include elements of it in my modern Chronicle, thanks to a Major Caern I'm using being a Museum secretly run by a sept of Glass Walkers and Children of Gaia, the inner part being exhibits based mostly around the savage ages, as well as the possibility of memory quests or even using Shattered Dreams Time Travel<br /> <br /> It's inspired me to similarly take elements from Shattered Dreams and Expand them more, in my case the Age of the Dragon Kings, Do you have any suggestions to offer on how to flesh out the era? Or did you have plans for that era?<br /> <br /> on my end the things I wanted to address were matters like<br /> while the sea reptiles, pterosaurs and Dinosaurs all got encompassed, what of the extant lizards and Crocodiles that were already there and clearly still encompassed by modern Mokole?<br /> What of the Snake Varna that eventually became the Nagah?<br /> Or the one that would eventually become the ancestors of all Bird Fera including the Corax?<br /> Attempting some stats for the varieties Saurid Varna<br /> maybe fleshing out other Era unique Fera, Primative mammals, amphibians of the times.<br /> How did they tackle the rise and fall of so many Species over the eons?<br /> <br /> back to Savage age, I came across apocryphal mentions of Falcon and Eagle Fera, Otters, Fresh Water fish and Were-Megatheriums, did you have any plans for them or would I be free to attempt a treatment of such things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","user":"Crazyjabberwock","date":". 05-21-2021, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-22T16:15:25-07:00","id":1449290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazyjabberwock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1449225#post1449225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">back to Savage age, I came across apocryphal mentions of Falcon and Eagle Fera, Otters, Fresh Water fish and Were-Megatheriums, did you have any plans for them or would I be free to attempt a treatment of such things?</div> </div> </div> </div>First off, I love hearing about people's ideas - especially when those ideas blend Apocalypse and Savage Age. <br /> <br /> Of that list, were-raptors are coming at some point (the Rapax) - which will be a book about &quot;redeeming&quot; the corax and expanding on their story options. Its a project &quot;in the pipe&quot; - so I have no idea when it will really evolve. We do have a Player's Guide in pretty good shape, which will talk about the canon Fera and how they fit into the Savage Age (including some notes about the Corax/Rapax).<br /> <br /> As to the others? Not so much. I have a few rules for new Fera for Savage Age -- one of which is that they generally need to come from apex predator stock. We will have some anwers about, ay, the were-otters, but it will be due to a case of mistaken identity rather than existing on their own. <br /> <br /> That said, its a big tent. They might not fit for Savage Age, but they could easily fit in an Apocalypse chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T09:38:07-07:00","id":1449353,"title":"","content":"I actually had a rough treatment for birds of prey before that, I'm sure yours is better, but this is what I had <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Raptryx: Warriors of the Sky<br /> <br /> tasked with Protecting and guiding messangers and spirits</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">F</span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">era derived from birds of prey such as the, </span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Owl,</span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"> Osprey, </span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Vulture, Condor,</span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"> Hawk, Falcon, Eagl</span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">e</span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\"> or Secretary Bird, </span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Of the ones who exist, they are divided by the specific types of raptors they are into various t</span><span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">ribes,</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">Once also had Flightless \u201cTerror\u201d bird breeds that have also gone extinct around the same time as the Khara, this demise was seen as a punishment for abandoning the sky</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">The Earliest of them branched off from the Dragon kings when Avian Dinosaurs started evolving to fly and compete with the Pterosaurs, In the Modern Day Metis Raptyx will often resemble these prehistoric proto-Birds</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">forms </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Liberation Serif, serif\">the standard Homid, \u201cRaptid\u201d (full bird) and Icharid(War Form), but also a charismatic \u201cHarpid\u201d form bearing a human face and a flightless but fearsome \u201cDromid\u201d form derived from some of the same ancient dreams the Mokole taught them about.</span><br /> <br /> I'm open to criticisms and if you like the ideas, you are free to them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-23T10:47:51-07:00","id":1449358,"title":"","content":"If we assume a single World of Darkness, it\u2019s always possible that any given rumored Changing Breeds are game of telephone references to other supernaturals. Fae most commonly.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s certainly what I\u2019d assume with otters and freshwater fish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T07:39:56-07:00","id":1449456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazyjabberwock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1449225#post1449225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have recently dived into all the Savage Age lore and will likely include elements of it in my modern Chronicle, thanks to a Major Caern I'm using being a Museum secretly run by a sept of Glass Walkers and Children of Gaia, the inner part being exhibits based mostly around the savage ages, as well as the possibility of memory quests or even using Shattered Dreams Time Travel<br /> <br /> It's inspired me to similarly take elements from Shattered Dreams and Expand them more, in my case the Age of the Dragon Kings, Do you have any suggestions to offer on how to flesh out the era? Or did you have plans for that era?<br /> <br /> on my end the things I wanted to address were matters like<br /> while the sea reptiles, pterosaurs and Dinosaurs all got encompassed, what of the extant lizards and Crocodiles that were already there and clearly still encompassed by modern Mokole?<br /> What of the Snake Varna that eventually became the Nagah?<br /> Or the one that would eventually become the ancestors of all Bird Fera including the Corax?<br /> Attempting some stats for the varieties Saurid Varna<br /> maybe fleshing out other Era unique Fera, Primative mammals, amphibians of the times.<br /> How did they tackle the rise and fall of so many Species over the eons?<br /> <br /> back to Savage age, I came across apocryphal mentions of Falcon and Eagle Fera, Otters, Fresh Water fish and Were-Megatheriums, did you have any plans for them or would I be free to attempt a treatment of such things?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Age of the Dragon Kings is one of my future projects for the Savage Age, need to clear the decks first.<br /> <br /> I plan on touching on the marine reptiles pre WonderWork, what we are calling Deep Time, in my oceans supplement, but yes there are separate Varna for the ichthyosaurs and sauropterygians. Ao and Kratii (sea snakes) varnas will show up in the Players Guide (coming soon), and we have made the Nagah part of the Mokole who split off a long time ago.<br /> <br /> \u200bCorax are being workd on as well, but I am not part of that project so you would need to get details from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11548_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11548\" data-vbnamecard=\"11548\">Coyoteintx</a> .<br /> <br /> The apocryphal Fera, I think, we are leaving alone for the most part, for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-24T09:15:00-07:00","id":1449464,"title":"","content":"Noted, I'll hold off on my own takes until I see what you make and probably incorporate it into my own projects later","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-23T07:15:24-07:00","id":1453271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1426329#post1426329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Christopher,Also I'd like to ask about these Cave Lions and Cave Bears -- how similar are they to the canon/modern Simba and Gurahl?<br /> And... have you considered making Bastet tribebooks for the Eurasian Qualmi/Werelynxes, and the <i>Miracinonyx</i> of North America? Or the Okuma?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I feel like I already asked you about your Ceilican but I can't find where. Are yours based on &quot;maneless lions&quot; or on some kinda wildcat?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you please clarify these for me?<br /> <br /> There were some very cool were-raptor projects started on ShadownEssence. The interpretations of their purpose for Gaia varied but always included being warriors of the skies, compared to Garou and Ajaba as warriors on the ground. One version included a strong prophetic part to their purpose: they are the primary recipients of prophecies of the future, and in addition to using that information for their own battles they were supposed to share that info with other Fera as necessary. I also connected my version to the Phoenix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 06-23-2021, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-30T17:42:40-07:00","id":1453877,"title":"","content":"How viable would it be to use Savage Age to run a Chronicle set in a Post-Post Apocalypse setting, like the green world type? the only issue I see is finding new ways to work in equivalents to the content that would be extinct in modern nights.<br /> <br /> on the other end I had been planning to make use of a Hollow Earth type setting to justify inclusion of Savage Age content in my modern chronicle, so maybe just explaining that whatever the Apocalypse was, opened very obvious passages to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:29:00-07:00","id":1454362,"title":"","content":"I think the vast majority of the material would be useful, with only real work needed being how to explain the &quot;simplified&quot; Umbra of the Savage Age, and the situation with the Triat. The simple Umbra could be as straightforward as it collapsed into a more condensed form (which coincidentally looks like the Savage Age Umbra) after whatever ELE happened in the Apocalypse. With the Trait, I think that would depend on the Apocalypse, who &quot;won&quot;, and what themes you would want to favor in your Post-Post setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T10:54:18-07:00","id":1454366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1454362#post1454362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> With the Trait, I think that would depend on the Apocalypse, who &quot;won&quot;, and what themes you would want to favor in your Post-Post setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I make no secret that Weaver Ascendant is my favored scenario and I'd use a version of that, so it would end with the wyrm and weaver healed, But the Wyld would go back to being the problem under the logic of &quot;look what THEY Did&quot; refusing to let any who remembered the old knowledge use it to innovate, she has no trust in anyone having learned any lessons and would try to reject even fetishcraft that resembles modern utilities, the followers of the Wyld here could be inspired by the Pure from WtF, because the Wyld was always mad to begin with.<br /> <br /> I had one other setting to use savage age content and that was the inner earth, and I could mix this with post apoc to justify the return of the various unique breeds from the apparent extinction they faced on the surface.<br /> <br /> Edit: I also thought it would be important to make not all tribes the same, for example the latest iteration of what was once the Glass Walkers could be re-born as something like &quot;The Scrap Riders&quot; or the &quot;Ruin Haunters&quot; or something like that, maybe resulting in them, getting a slight mad Max Flavor to contrast the more prehistoric flavored elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26780,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","user":"Crazyjabberwock","date":". 07-14-2021, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-14T20:31:45-07:00","id":1454939,"title":"","content":"I was pondering Enemies for a Savage Age Chronicle, Any plans for stats for Savage Vampires? I'm not super into VtM but they make absolutely splendid antagonists when one tires of fighting Banes, Fomori and the usual suspects","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-19T13:35:47-07:00","id":1455212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coyoteintx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1449290#post1449290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First off, I love hearing about people's ideas - especially when those ideas blend Apocalypse and Savage Age.<br /> <br /> Of that list, were-raptors are coming at some point (the Rapax) - which will be a book about &quot;redeeming&quot; the corax and expanding on their story options. Its a project &quot;in the pipe&quot; - so I have no idea when it will really evolve. We do have a Player's Guide in pretty good shape, which will talk about the canon Fera and how they fit into the Savage Age (including some notes about the Corax/Rapax).<br /> <br /> As to the others? Not so much. I have a few rules for new Fera for Savage Age -- one of which is that they generally need to come from apex predator stock. We will have some anwers about, ay, the were-otters, but it will be due to a case of mistaken identity rather than existing on their own.<br /> <br /> That said, its a big tent. They might not fit for Savage Age, but they could easily fit in an Apocalypse chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sorry for questioning constantly, do the Rapax also encompass things like Flightless Birds that were often Apex predators in some Regions? or are they likely to be their own thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26780-crazyjabberwock","name":"Crazyjabberwock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26780_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T06:54:50-07:00","id":1455250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazyjabberwock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1454939#post1454939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was pondering Enemies for a Savage Age Chronicle, Any plans for stats for Savage Vampires? I'm not super into VtM but they make absolutely splendid antagonists when one tires of fighting Banes, Fomori and the usual suspects</div> </div> </div> </div>The general consensus of the writing team is that the Vampires of V:tM are not around in the Savage Age, for two reasons. One, Caine was a farmer and agriculture is just barely getting started at the end of the Savage Age. Two, vampires in our conception of the Savage Age and W:tA are not the vampires of V:tM, they are people that are possessed by blood drinking spirits.<br /> <br /> Crossovers in general are all going to be heavily filtered though a Werewolf lens and little explicit mention will be made using terms from other games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-20T06:58:57-07:00","id":1455251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crazyjabberwock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1361893-intro-and-the-savage-age?p=1455212#post1455212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Sorry for questioning constantly, do the Rapax also encompass things like Flightless Birds that were often Apex predators in some Regions? or are they likely to be their own thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>No problem, we like questions! If you do the Discord thing we have a fairly active community there. PM me for an invite.<br /> <br /> I'll let <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11548_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11548\" data-vbnamecard=\"11548\">Coyoteintx</a> field the Rapax question, as he is doing the writing for it. My guess would be that the Phorusrhacids would be a separate thing. Last I had heard was the Rapax were going to draw more from Maniraptora for visual inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/c